5.2 Silicon Removal Thermodynamics

The Gibbs free energy change for the reaction

\mathrm{Si + 2CaO + 2CO \rightarrow Ca_2SiO_4 + 2C}

at 1773 K is calculated from standard formation data as \Delta G = -150 kJ mol⁻¹, confirming spontaneity. By injecting 0.15 kg CaO into the melt, 0.10 kg of Si (present at 3 wt% in a 3.5 kg alloy) can be oxidised, reducing the silicon content to below 0.3 wt%. The slag mass increases correspondingly. Without this Zone 4 step, the product would be a brittle Fe‑Si alloy unsuitable for structural applications; with it, the Phase 1 target Fe‑0.2C‑2.0Ni is achievable.

